# Exclusions for pulling a compute node's checkout back to the dev machine.
#
#   rsync -av -e "ssh -T" --exclude-from=.rsync-exclude-pull \
#         USER@HOST:~/payne-zero/ ./
#
# This file exists because `.rsync-exclude` is **push-direction only**. That
# file excludes `runs/`, `results/` and `*.log` so a code push does not clobber
# remote results -- which is exactly the payload of a pull. Using it here
# silently transfers nothing but source, and rsync reports success. See
# solver-in-the-loop-cluster.md section 8.
#
# Everything not listed here comes back: code, notes, runs/, results/,
# figures/, artifacts/, logs/.

# Both sides have their own. The remote's is Linux; the local one is macOS.
.git/
.venv/
.venv-linux/
.cache/

# 6.9 GB of static catalogs, already present locally. But note the exception:
# corpora *generated* on the remote live under this prefix too and will be
# missed. After a pull, check for remote-only files with
#   rsync -avn --ignore-existing HOST:.../source_data_files/ source_data_files/
# and fetch them by name. This is how strict_truth_52199.npz (199 MB) was
# nearly left behind.
source_data_files/

# A second, root-level copy of the same four catalog trees -- a further 6.9 GB,
# real directories rather than symlinks. Measured on Node-06, 2026-08-08:
#   source_catalogs 6.8G   atmosphere_emulator 131M
#   synthesis_tables 866K  atmosphere_tables 443K
# Excluding only `source_data_files/` is therefore not enough; without these
# four the pull drags the catalogs back a second time under new paths. The
# leading slash anchors each to the transfer root, so a *nested*
# `source_data_files/atmosphere_emulator/` is unaffected by these rules.
/atmosphere_emulator/
/atmosphere_tables/
/source_catalogs/
/synthesis_tables/

# Per-machine agent state, not project content.
.claude/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.DS_Store
tmp/
tutorial_output/
